{% comment %}
  Renders a product's customer-facing price (Slice 2B / owner §3, criterion 56).

  This snippet is the SHARED price renderer for the whole theme — PDP, cards,
  search (docs/specs/SLICE-2B-CART-SURFACE-INVENTORY.md E1). It intentionally
  no longer renders Dawn's native "regular / sale" price by default: every
  caller in this theme now passes an explicit `mode`, because a caller that
  fell through to an undeclared default here would silently render a bare
  Shopify price where a Bank Payment figure was expected — exactly the wrong
  kind of "looks correct in review" failure this stage exists to prevent.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object
  - mode: {String} REQUIRED. One of:
      'as_low_as' — collection/search discovery cards (owner §3 "collection
        and search"). Reads the PRODUCT-LEVEL `carat.as_low_as_bank_minor_units`
        metafield (R13/R9) and shows "As low as $X" labelled as the Bank
        Payment Price. Never shows the Regular/Card Price. Renders the
        unavailable state — never a stale or fallback figure — on ANY of:
        the metafield being absent (R14/P2 — the backend actively DELETES
        this metafield, rather than leaving it stale, the moment no variant
        is currently purchasable, so absence is itself meaningful, not just
        "not written yet"), the embedded source variant not being found or
        not currently `available`, or its `cardPriceAnchorMinorUnits` no
        longer matching that variant's live Shopify price (R14, see below).
      'pdp'       — product detail page (owner §3 "Product page"). Reads the
        VARIANT-LEVEL `carat.bank_payment_price_minor_units` metafield.
        Shows the Regular/Card Price — always the native Shopify
        `variant.price`, i.e. what checkout will actually charge — as the
        primary figure. Shows the Bank Payment Price and the exact dollar
        saving alongside ONLY when the metafield's `shopifyVariantId` names
        the variant being rendered AND its `cardPriceAnchorMinorUnits`
        agrees with that variant's live native price (criterion 56 /
        R14's coherence rule, see below). On any mismatch — including the
        metafield being entirely absent — renders the card price alone.
  - use_variant: {Boolean} Selects `product.selected_or_first_available_variant`
    as the pricing target. Required (and forced) for 'pdp' mode; ignored by
    'as_low_as' mode, which is always product-level.
  - placeholder: {Boolean} Onboarding/theme-editor placeholder only (no real
    product selected) — renders placeholder figures, never real customer data.
  - show_badges: {Boolean} Renders 'Sale' and 'Sold Out' tags (optional,
    'pdp' mode only — see below for why 'as_low_as' does not use this).
  - price_class: {String} Adds a price class to the price element (optional)

  WHY 'as_low_as' DROPS THE NATIVE compare_at_price "on sale" TREATMENT THAT
  THIS SNIPPET USED TO RENDER FOR CARDS. `compare_at_price` and `variant.price`
  are both Card-basis Shopify fields. Showing that native "was $X" strike-
  through beside a Bank-Payment-basis headline price would silently pair a
  Card-basis figure with a Bank-basis one with no label distinguishing them —
  the same class of mismatched-pair error criterion 56 exists to prevent,
  just introduced by a different native feature instead of a sync failure.
  'pdp' mode keeps the Sale/Sold-out badges because there both figures it
  touches (`compare_at_price`, `variant.price`) are Card-basis — an
  apples-to-apples comparison that never touches the Bank Payment pair.

  THE R14 COHERENCE CHECK — A SELF-VALIDATING ANCHOR, VERIFIED AGAINST THE
  LIVE STORE, NOT DERIVED. Earlier revisions of this file compared the
  metafield's OWN `regularCardPriceMinorUnits`/`bankPaymentPriceMinorUnits`
  against the native price, because the only identity in the payload
  (`masterVariantId`) is this app's internal Postgres id — NOT a Shopify
  variant id/GID — and Liquid has no way to resolve that against
  `product.variants`. The owner's R14 ruling closed that gap by having the
  backend embed TWO PURPOSE-BUILT fields alongside the display figures:
  `shopifyVariantId` (the exact value Liquid's own `variant.id` returns,
  confirmed against the live `ProductVariant.legacyResourceId`) and
  `cardPriceAnchorMinorUnits` (a Card price snapshot in the same
  raw-integer-minor-units form `variant.price` already is). Both are
  decimal STRINGS, like every other field in this payload — an initial
  number-typed version was rejected by the architect as an unnecessary
  money-safety exemption — so both get the same `| plus: 0` numeric-cast
  idiom already used for the display figures before comparing. Both fields
  exist ONLY to validate the pair; never render either.
  A metafield write can fail independently of the native price write and
  leave an OLD value that is internally self-consistent (its own
  `priceCalculationId` really was published once) — criterion 56's naive
  "does the metafield agree with itself" framing would miss that. This
  anchor closes it: the native price mutation succeeded, so Shopify's own
  live `variant.price` already moved, and the stale anchor no longer equals
  it. The check needs no extra failure signal because it is always compared
  against the one value that cannot itself be stale — what Shopify is
  currently serving.

  Usage:
  {% render 'price', product: product, mode: 'as_low_as' %}
  {% render 'price', product: product, mode: 'pdp', use_variant: true, show_badges: true %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  if mode == 'pdp' or use_variant
    assign target = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  elsif placeholder
    assign target = null
  else
    assign target = product
  endif

  assign compare_at_price = target.compare_at_price
  assign price = target.price | default: 1999
  assign available = target.available | default: false
-%}

{%- if mode == 'as_low_as' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign as_low_as_metafield = product.metafields.carat.as_low_as_bank_minor_units.value
    assign as_low_as_bank_minor = as_low_as_metafield.bankPaymentPriceMinorUnits | plus: 0
    assign as_low_as_metafield_variant_id = as_low_as_metafield.shopifyVariantId | plus: 0
    assign as_low_as_metafield_card_anchor_minor = as_low_as_metafield.cardPriceAnchorMinorUnits | plus: 0

    comment
      R14 / P2. `as_low_as_metafield` being nil is ITSELF meaningful, not just
      "not written yet": the backend actively DELETES this metafield the
      moment no variant is currently purchasable, rather than leaving a
      stale value behind. So the `!= blank` check below already covers that
      case correctly with no separate "never written" branch needed.

      The `for` loop resolves the metafield's `shopifyVariantId` — a real
      Liquid-native variant id, unlike the internal-only `masterVariantId` —
      against this product's actual variants, so the purchasability and
      price-freshness checks below are an EXACT per-variant check, not the
      coarse product-level proxy this file used before R14. `shopifyVariantId`
      and `cardPriceAnchorMinorUnits` are decimal strings like every other
      field in this payload (an earlier number-typed draft was rejected by
      the architect), so both get the same `| plus: 0` cast as the display
      figures before comparing — assigned once above rather than inline in
      the `if`/`for` conditions below, to keep operator precedence unambiguous.
    endcomment

    assign as_low_as_source_variant = null
    unless as_low_as_metafield == blank
      for v in product.variants
        if v.id == as_low_as_metafield_variant_id
          assign as_low_as_source_variant = v
        endif
      endfor
    endunless

    assign as_low_as_purchasable = false
    if placeholder == null and as_low_as_metafield != blank and as_low_as_source_variant != null and as_low_as_source_variant.available and as_low_as_source_variant.price == as_low_as_metafield_card_anchor_minor and as_low_as_bank_minor > 0
      assign as_low_as_purchasable = true
    endif

    if settings.currency_code_enabled
      assign as_low_as_money = as_low_as_bank_minor | money_with_currency
    else
      assign as_low_as_money = as_low_as_bank_minor | money
    endif
  -%}
  <div
    class="
      price
      {%- if price_class %} {{ price_class }}{% endif -%}
      {%- if as_low_as_purchasable == false and placeholder == null %} price--sold-out{% endif -%}
    "
  >
    <div class="price__container">
      {%- if as_low_as_purchasable -%}
        <div class="price__regular">
          <span class="price-item price-item--regular carat-as-low-as">
            {{- 'products.product.price.as_low_as_html' | t: price: as_low_as_money -}}
          </span>
          <span class="caption carat-as-low-as__label">
            {{- 'products.product.price.bank_payment_price' | t -}}
          </span>
        </div>
      {%- elsif placeholder -%}
        {%- comment -%} Onboarding/theme-editor placeholder only — never real customer data. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign placeholder_money = 1999 | money -%}
        <div class="price__regular">
          <span class="price-item price-item--regular carat-as-low-as">
            {{- 'products.product.price.as_low_as_html' | t: price: placeholder_money -}}
          </span>
          <span class="caption carat-as-low-as__label">
            {{- 'products.product.price.bank_payment_price' | t -}}
          </span>
        </div>
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="price-item price-item--unavailable">
          {{- 'products.product.price.as_low_as_unavailable' | t -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- elsif mode == 'pdp' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign native_card_minor = target.price
    assign bank_metafield = target.metafields.carat.bank_payment_price_minor_units.value
    assign metafield_bank_minor = bank_metafield.bankPaymentPriceMinorUnits | plus: 0
    assign metafield_saving_minor = bank_metafield.bankPaymentSavingsMinorUnits | plus: 0
    assign bank_metafield_variant_id = bank_metafield.shopifyVariantId | plus: 0
    assign bank_metafield_card_anchor_minor = bank_metafield.cardPriceAnchorMinorUnits | plus: 0

    comment
      R14. `shopifyVariantId` and `cardPriceAnchorMinorUnits` exist ONLY to
      validate this pair — never rendered. Both are decimal strings like
      every other field in this payload (an earlier number-typed draft was
      rejected by the architect), so both get the same `| plus: 0` cast used
      for the display figures — assigned once above rather than inline in
      the `if` condition below, to keep operator precedence unambiguous —
      before comparing against `target.id` / `native_card_minor`.
    endcomment

    assign bank_pair_coherent = false
    if placeholder == null and bank_metafield != blank and bank_metafield_variant_id == target.id and bank_metafield_card_anchor_minor == native_card_minor
      assign bank_pair_coherent = true
    endif

    if settings.currency_code_enabled
      assign card_money = native_card_minor | money_with_currency
      assign bank_money = metafield_bank_minor | money_with_currency
      assign saving_money = metafield_saving_minor | money_with_currency
    else
      assign card_money = native_card_minor | money
      assign bank_money = metafield_bank_minor | money
      assign saving_money = metafield_saving_minor | money
    endif
  -%}
  <div
    class="
      price
      {%- if price_class %} {{ price_class }}{% endif -%}
      {%- if available == false %} price--sold-out{% endif -%}
      {%- if compare_at_price > price %} price--on-sale{% endif -%}
      {%- if show_badges %} price--show-badge{% endif -%}
    "
  >
    <div class="price__container">
      <div class="price__regular">
        <span class="visually-hidden visually-hidden--inline">{{ 'products.product.price.regular_price' | t }}</span>
        <span class="price-item price-item--regular carat-card-price">
          {%- if placeholder -%}
            {{- 1999 | money -}}
          {%- else -%}
            {{- card_money -}}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- if compare_at_price > price -%}
          <span class="visually-hidden visually-hidden--inline">
            {{- 'products.product.price.regular_price' | t -}}
          </span>
          <s class="price-item price-item--regular variant-item__old-price">
            {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
              {{- compare_at_price | money_with_currency -}}
            {%- else -%}
              {{- compare_at_price | money -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          </s>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if bank_pair_coherent -%}
        <div class="carat-bank-payment-pair">
          <div class="carat-bank-payment-price">
            <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.price.bank_payment_price' | t }}:</span>
            <span class="price-item price-item--bank-payment">{{ bank_money }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="carat-bank-payment-saving">
            {{- 'products.product.price.bank_payment_saving_html' | t: amount: saving_money -}}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- unless placeholder -%}
        {%- if target.unit_price_measurement -%}
          {% render 'unit-price', price: target.unit_price, measurement: target.unit_price_measurement %}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endunless -%}
    </div>
    {%- if show_badges -%}
      <span class="badge price__badge-sale color-{{ settings.sale_badge_color_scheme }}">
        {{ 'products.product.on_sale' | t }}
      </span>

      <span class="badge price__badge-sold-out color-{{ settings.sold_out_badge_color_scheme }}">
        {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
